WEBVTT

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:15.960
“In order for the Sabbath to heal one's heart, one must work diligently on the other six days.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.880
Even God, our creator, is no exception”

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.370
— Kirk H. Hill

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.880
Arashiyama, you have plenty of qualities that Tatsuno can't compete with.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.430
I know that for a fact.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:16.080
Darn it! My mind keeps wandering to Mr. Moriaki!

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.150
And my fantasies are starting to override my memories!

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:23.250
It's finally Sunday, so I shouldn't be thinking about school or teachers!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.630
Today, I'm gonna buckle down and finish my book.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.970
Stop right there!

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.920
Take a closer look.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.220
You're holding a chikuwa!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.720
Normally, nobody would mistake it for a stick of dynamite!

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.650
Except for the culprit!

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:50.450
This sucks! Why do I keep picturing Mr. Moriaki as the main character?!

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.780
Why...

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:58.450
Ow!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.290
Hey sis, play with me!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.830
Sis is busy right now.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.170
Liar! You were just sitting there daydreaming!

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.100
Daydreaming is part of being a grown-up.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:19.050
All right now, Yukiko. Be a good girl and play with your brother.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.350
Takeru, play with Yukiko!

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:24.890
What?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.650
Come on, you've got some two-player games, don't you?

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.520
Like “Mario Sisters” or something.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.070
What're you doing?!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.150
I didn't even save!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.550
Hey, knock it off!

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.780
This is all your fault!

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.630
Mom! Hotori's being mean!

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.770
Hotori, what did you do!?

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.510
Argh! That's it!

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.350
You girls are supposed to be off today.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.350
What are you doing here?

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.270
I just get in trouble if I stay home.

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.560
I came just in case Sanada-kun decided to stop by!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.420
Sanada?

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.490
Tatsuno-san's a healthy young girl.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:14.280
Hotori, on the other hand...

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.070
Anyway, get this, Tatsuno-san.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:22.530
Lately when I think of Mr. Moriaki, I get a funny feeling right here.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.700
Oh my! Hotori's in love too?

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.290
Tell me about it.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:30.120
Just thinking about that math test makes me sick to my stomach.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.710
I didn't mean my stomach.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:37.570
I can't make head or tails out of stuff like differentials and integrals!

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.920
Iffegrals and Diffigentles?

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.090
<i>Differentials</i> and <i>integrals</i>.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.100
I can't understand any of that complicated stuff!

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.560
I couldn't even make it past dividing with fractions!

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.250
I thought it'd work if you just flipped 'em over...

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.860
I'm still not sure I really get it.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.190
I'm amazed you've made it to high school.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.220
Seems like Tatsuno's not exactly suited for giving advice.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:06.680
Hotori didn't even notice the subject change from love problems to math, though...

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:11.670
Well, don't they say that kids who have their
fractions down, make it through life just fine?

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.840
Yeah! I saw that movie too!

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.280
Even if you don't have the book smarts,

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.310
you're fine if you can just see eye to eye with people.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.130
And coast through life that way.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.840
Even life has its own formula, huh?

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.870
Now we're talking about the meaning of life!

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.980
Just kick reason to the curb and live like that, and you'll be fine, y'know?

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.880
Like with the perps in those cartoon detective shows.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:35.610
Even if your deductive reasoning isn't good, you can guess the perp just by using the formula.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.360
Really?! What formula?

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:42.440
It's whatever character the top billing voice actor plays!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.370
Aww, I shouldn't have asked!

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.870
Now I'll know next time!

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:53.140
Hey Hotori, since you're free, go down to the
grocery store and get me some potatoes and onions.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.960
But today I'm just a customer.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.050
Then pay your bill and go home!

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:02.660
Tch! Fine, I'll go, so let me borrow it.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.050
The vroom-vroom thingy.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.510
Woo-hoo!

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:14.210
Potatoes 'n onions, potatoes 'n onions!

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.060
Potatoes...

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:18.610
H-HEY!!!

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.990
Potatoooes!

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:22.740
On...

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.240
Onio...

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.940
...ions!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.870
Cripes!

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.830
Hey, that's dangerous, you know!

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.050
Jeez, what's your problem?

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:42.550
You just ignore people when they tell you to stop?

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:47.050
Sheesh. People like you remind me that spring time absent-mindedness is in full bloom.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.350
YOU'RE THE DANGEROUS ONE HERE!

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:52.560
I just bumped into you!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:56.460
Women have no idea how much this hurts!

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.470
It's your fault for jumping out in front of me anyway.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:00.400
This is all <i>your</i> fault!

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.110
I've told you before not to ride that down this street!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.280
Keep it up, and I'll declare this an accident-related injury!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.930
Don't ride on the street?

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.740
So what, am I supposed to ride it inside my house then?

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.750
My mom would wring my neck!

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.920
Why you little!

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.380
You respect your mother more than the law?

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:24.110
This is why I hate kids.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:24.970
Listen to me!

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:28.300
No driver's license, no license plate, no headlights,

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.430
and no blinker either!

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:34.120
For these reasons, you cannot ride that on this street!

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:40.230
You can't eat a burger without the meat, cheese, lettuce or pickles, right?

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:43.990
You can still have the bun.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.170
All right, that's it.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:50.450
Hmph. Fine, I won't ride it anymore.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.580
What gives? You're awfully cooperative today.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.960
I'm already there anyway.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.960
Nothing's better than a bean paste bun and a glass of milk.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.340
Oh, you running errands for the old hag?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.130
I'll be sure to tell her you said that.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.730
We got fresh carrots, straight from Kouchi!

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.540
Fresh outta the ground! Still got dirt on 'em! Come one, come all!

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:21.010
Umm, I think it was curry ingredients or something...

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.190
Oh yeah, it was potatoes and...

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.490
Potatoes and...

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.090
...carrots please.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:33.400
Thanks for shoppin'!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.330
Oh yeah, Hotori-chan.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.000
Take this back with ya.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.970
It expires tomorrow, but you could clear it by then, right?

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.500
Wow, thanks!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:48.490
Heh. Drinking that might help you get a little bigger!

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:50.800
Got that right!

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.890
What might get bigger!?

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:57.090
I oughta sue for sexual harassment!

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.570
Hey Mr. Policeman, stop laughing and and reprimand him!

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.400
Yes ma'am!

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.400
I wanna live life smiling.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.400
Perverted geezers. I won't forget this!

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:12.530
Don't ride that. Walk it back, please.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.530
Headlights and a license plate, right?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.870
And the blinkers <i>and</i> driver's license!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.670
Don't try to cut corners, or I'll confiscate it!

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:23.500
Forget it. You're too high-strung to handle it.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:24.500
Huh?

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.250
Let's ride, Tetsuo!

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:31.090
There's no Tetsuo he- I SAID DON'T RIDE IT!

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.980
For Pete's sake!

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.640
Someday she'll leave her nest and get married...

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:41.530
Then the town can extinguish that fire.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.650
It's still raging right now, though.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.360
I'm back!

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:54.820
Sanada actually came!

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:55.870
Huh?

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:57.870
Aww, back so soon?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.950
Took you long enough.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.120
But that cop was threatening to arrest me.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.670
What'd you do?

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.040
I had an incomplete hamburger.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.870
Good work. Want some coffee?

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:14.090
Just a cup, please. I'm gonna have some milk.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:18.890
What's up, you trying to get bigger?

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.960
No point in trying now. You've already passed your growing stage.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.520
It's no big deal if you're a little small.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:31.400
That's what makes you you. You're fine just the way you-

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:37.620
Why does everyone have to mention my boobs?! Huh?!

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.120
That does it! I'm suing for sexual harassment!

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.990
W-wait, objection! I was talking about your height...

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.330
Yeah! Sanada-kun's not that kind of person!

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.710
The audience may not interject with opinions!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.630
Objection! I'll represent Sanada-kun.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.180
Overruled!

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:57.510
I'm telling you, I meant your height, not your boobs!

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:00.320
I told her to get potatoes and <i>onions</i>!

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.110
You have the right to remain silent.

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:06.500
Anything you say can and will he held against you in a court of law, got it?

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.110
That's when you arrest someone, not when they're on trial!

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.530
Arrest... trial... who cares?

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:14.110
You're in contempt of court!

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:17.070
“Spin city” for short.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.660
What's the world coming to?

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.290
Maid-you!

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.540
What's that?

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:26.750
I just changed thank you to maid-you.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.130
But what's that got to do with the Vulcan salute?

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.580
It's different!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.250
Vulcans do this.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.720
This is maid-you. The thumb makes it an M.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:39.430
If we make this the shop's greeting, we'll attract more customers!

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:43.100
You imbecile. How would that bring in customers?

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:46.350
Mai... Hey, I can't do it!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.440
Doesn't matter. Rejected.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:52.360
But if we don't have a unique flair, nobody will come!

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:00.540
Head Maid, look at this!

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.700
Your stupidity is what's keeping them away!

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:09.060
Our world is a mirror that reflects your true nature.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:12.710
A peaceful world reflects a loving heart,

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:17.220
but in tough times, the seas of
adversity are caught in a whirlpool.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.470
Another one.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.680
Here's another arrow.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.160
Here too.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.190
Hey, you're from the cleaner's aren't ya?

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:34.650
What's going on here, guys?

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.960
Well, these arrows are posted all over town.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:41.660
Ah, to tell the truth, I've been following these myself.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.490
Is there some kind of event going on?

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.250
Hey, look!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.210
It's the old hag's place.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.250
Yo!

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:57.570
Great. More tough guys.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:58.460
Welcome ho-

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.030
MAID-YOU!

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:01.300
This place has no sense of coordination.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.100
Hey granny, what's with all the arrows?

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:06.580
You guys planning something?

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.600
What arrows? This is news to me.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.230
That's my genius design!

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:19.820
I spent two whole days posting these around town to attract customers.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.030
At times, like a ninja.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.580
At others, like a shinobi.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.330
They're the same thing.

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.120
Like that would actually get anyone to come!

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:33.210
It did.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:34.840
Crap, it did!

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.230
Whatever, we'll just discuss the festival plans here.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:43.480
Yeah, we're already here anyway.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.490
3 waters!

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.660
3 waters, coming right up!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.220
3 coffees, got it!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.900
3 cutlet curries comin' up.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.860
They're blatantly screwing it up!

00:13:58.920 --> 00:13:59.860
Excuse me...

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:00.690
Hey there.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:01.820
Welcome home, Ma-

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.530
Maid-you!

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:03.570
Um, about these arrows...

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:09.640
Another victim! We should change “café” to “Antlion's nest”!

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.370
Not a chance.

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.670
I figured it was you.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:16.380
Hey, why'd you take them down? You stupid four-eyed cop!

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.250
Bifocop!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:21.030
You can't just go around posting these things.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:22.380
There were thirty of them!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:29.370
I worked so hard on those! Why do you hate me so much?!

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:31.730
That's not why I did it.

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:37.480
Whenever I act out of concern for this town, I end up butting heads with you.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.810
Do you have to be a constant obstruction in my life?!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.030
I could say the same to you.

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:47.150
Terribly sorry. Our maid here is such a moron.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.290
Please help yourself to a cold drink.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:55.170
Gnaw on some ice and crawl back into your cave!

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:55.920
Beat it! Scram!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.960
I've had it with you...

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:01.230
I told you not to mouth off...

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.970
...to the customer!

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.430
Got it? Don't blame me if I shoot you next time.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:19.900
Stupid jerk!

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:24.200
Was that a Beat Takeshi impression?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.450
Yeesh, that was terrible.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.330
What?! I dare you to say that again!

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:36.080
What'd you call me!?

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:42.300
Oh? So then you chased them around town for half an hour?

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:45.020
What do we do with her, Head Maid?

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:47.220
Considering the situation, and no valid excuse...

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.320
30 minute's pay cut.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.250
How come?! I'm busting my hump here!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.130
“Busting your hump” chasing middle schoolers will get you arrested.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.980
No, before that! Like my original greeting and the flyers!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.070
I'm trying to attract classier patrons.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:03.820
I mean, look at this freak show.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.790
Hey! What're you blaming <i>us</i> for?!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:11.530
We're supporting your business by eating right before dinner!

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.780
Yeah! Now I won't be able to finish supper tonight!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.160
What am I supposed to say to my family?

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:20.170
Jeez, bunch of family-obsessed weenies.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:24.070
Well, I do understand what Arashiyama's trying to say.

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:26.760
The place has kind of been in a rut lately.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:32.140
Our only customers are regulars from the shopping district.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:35.890
We need customers who truly appreciate maids.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:39.400
Why the hell are you blaming us?!

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:44.460
But so far, none of Arashiyama-san's ideas have worked.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:46.550
Especially that insufferable greeting!

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:50.630
Fine, but we should at least try to make the store eye-catching.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:54.240
Yeah, our makeshift sign isn't exactly up to snuff.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:58.760
We ought to just have a new sign made.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:16:59.920
Good idea!

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:07.880
That little crybaby that I treated like my own granddaughter is telling me how to run my store!

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.600
Oh, what's the matter Hotori-chan, dear?

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:18.890
There, there, have some curry, hon.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.830
I ended up not giving him any chocolate...

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.230
I'm such a chicken!

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:28.280
There, there, have some curry, hon.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.110
I'm crying 'cause I lost my purse!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:36.470
There, there, have some curry, hon.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:40.040
Granny, what are you wearing?! Did you finally lose it?!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:43.080
Maid café's are a lucrative business these days.

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:46.630
Here, have some curry.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:53.140
You're enjoying that, aren't you, Hotori?

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.520
I've got a proposition for you.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:05.060
I'll forget about the 10 years worth of free curry if you work here for me.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.190
What?!

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.900
That little crybaby that I treated like my own granddaughter...

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.080
I'll deal with the sign eventually,

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.820
But I'm all for making the place stand out.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.470
Let's give it a shot.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:19.400
Really?

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.340
But how do we do that?

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:24.440
Hmm. Well, I got a big ol' sheet upstairs...

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:26.840
Why don't you make a flashy banner out of it?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.320
This is gonna be a lot of fun!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.510
Hey, you better take this seriously.

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:39.770
Found it! Here we are.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.520
There's some paint here too.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.390
What are you going to write?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:52.030
For starters, I'll write “Maid Café Seaside” in huge letters.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:54.200
Can you even write the kanji for café?

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.490
I can, thank you!

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:57.820
Here goes!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.640
You talk big, but it ended up like crap.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:12.550
It's very “you”.

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:17.680
Let me borrow the paint. I'll write “sophisticated” in the blank space.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:19.970
Won't we get sued by an advertising committee?

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.350
Don't worry. It's not a big deal.

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:24.940
Here we go!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.810
Perfect!

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.530
Nice, Tattsun!

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:36.570
Milk is perfect with saucy cutlet bowls.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.020
Make sure to stretch it all the way!

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:40.580
Got it!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.160
Done!

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.930
Granny, come check it out!

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.440
It's a work of art!

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.710
Oh, I can't wait to see it.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.430
Ta-daa!

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:03.430
Childish...

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.100
Damn you, Naito Dentistry!

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:11.400
It's like the whole world's out to get me today!

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:12.730
Damn you, world!

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:18.560
Our world is a mirror that reflects your true nature.

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:22.310
A peaceful world reflects a loving heart,

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:27.590
but in tough times, the seas of adversity are caught in a whirlpool.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.610
I'll tear this thing down,

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:32.790
and triumph over society!

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:38.150
You're supposed to do these things at night, Arashiyama-san.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.960
Just like a ninja, or a shinobi.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.140
Do what like a shinobi?

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:48.310
What, pray tell, are you doing to my sign?

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:58.750
We're sorry. That was very childish of us.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:03.030
Keep pulling stunts like this oughta attract some folks.

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:31.580
Thank you very maid for coming!

00:22:34.730 --> 00:22:40.280
So when you returned to the store, the victim was already dead, is that it?!

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:43.170
Suspect A is the pretty boutique owner.

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:46.130
Suspect B is the driver of the taxi she rode.

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:50.560
Suspect C is the IT exec with investments in said boutique.

00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:54.560
The pretty lady's voice is kind of cute. Sounds like she'd be popular...

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:59.440
But the taxi driver's kind of shady and has a raspy voice.

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:03.840
The IT exec's definitely in an affair with the pretty lady.

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:07.840
No, wait. His voice is charming, and popular-sounding too.

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:11.210
Who's the highest billing voice actor of the three?

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:16.870
Don't tell me you think Sachiko-san did it!

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:18.620
He's the culprit!

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:21.040
Wha... How'd you know?

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:24.130
He's just pretending to be dead.

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:27.330
But they haven't said it yet. How'd you know?

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:29.010
'Cause it's a rerun!

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:40.750
Mom! Hotori's being mean again!

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:42.500
Hotori, what did you do!?

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:44.980
Ahh, jeez!

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:50.180
There's no year of the cat in the Chinese Zodiac, is there?

00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:52.390
There are no cat constellations either.

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:54.770
Why isn't there one for such an ordinary animal?

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:57.540
Well, some folks have names like Nekodzuka or Nekozaki, though.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:24:01.550
But what about Tatsuno Toshiko? Dragons don't even exist!

00:24:01.550 --> 00:24:03.650
Maybe it's so ordinary they just forgot?

00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:05.530
I smell a rat.

00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:10.070
I bet there's an ugly truth behind the exclusion of the cat year!

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:10.570
Next time!

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:12.570
3rd Street: The Cat Boy.

00:24:12.570 --> 00:24:15.110
The city'll still be turning tomorrow.
